  "facts": [
    "The Marine Parkway–Gil Hodges Memorial Bridge, opened July 3, 1937, once held the title of the world's longest vertical‑lift vehicular span, stretching 540 feet across Rockaway Inlet.",
    "Designed by David B. Steinman, the bridge’s twin towers house the lift machinery and feature whimsical curled tops, a signature aesthetic that has made it an iconic Rockaway landmark.",
    "Renovated 1999‑2001, the bridge’s four lanes were widened, a new steel grating installed, and a Jersey barrier added, all while preserving its historic lift span and pedestrian walkway."
  ],
